<title>FRANCE: Snecma sees two years strong growth.</title>
<headline>Snecma sees two years strong growth.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-02-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Turnover at French aircraft engine maker Snecma should rise significantly this year and next, French financial daily La Tribune reported on Monday.</p>
<p>Citing company sources, the paper said Snecma's turnover would rise almost 40 percent to 12.5 billion francs in 1997 and a further 10.4 percent to 13.8 billion francs next year.</p>
<p>No one was immediately available at the company to comment on the report.</p>
<p>The newspaper said the company's production of CFM56 jet engines, which it produces with General Electric, would rise to 770 this year and 920 in 1998, from 440 in 1996.</p>
